doc.details:
Desktop calls and listener registration are UI-thread only; mobile backends marshal calls to the host UI thread. Reads complete exactly once, on a later UI-loop turn, and require a running host event loop. A callback's first argument is false on access, conversion or concurrent-change failure; its second argument is then default-initialized. Missing formats are successful reads. Notifications may be coalesced and contain no clipboard content. Subscribing does not emit an initial event. Writes replace every previous format and retain copies. Native commit failures may leave the clipboard empty or partially updated.

```cpp
auto& clipboard = Clipboard::GetInstance();
ClipboardData data;
data.text = "Hello";
data.html = "<b>Hello</b>";
clipboard.Write(data);
clipboard.ReadText([](bool success, std::optional<std::string> text) {
  if (success && text) { }
});
```

